Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The guard read a claim with no ending after it as "an agent is working", and
a claim outlives its run whenever a run dies without reporting. On such a node
the guard removed every comment a person wrote and nothing ever healed the
thread — the jam #12 was stuck in, where `/atomaton recover` was deleted twice.

The run the claim names is now asked about directly. Only the answered
`completed` counts as stale: an unreadable status keeps the old behaviour
(deleting), and a park is never stale here because the aggregation resumes it
and reads what was written during the wait. Keeping the comment also lets the
dispatch take it up, which is the way back in.
